{
    "_comment": [
        "Input for sif_sprite_packer (see sif/tools/Sprite_Packer.cpp).",
        "",
        "The art pack ships one PNG per animation frame; PrimitiveAnimation wants",
        "frames as rectangles inside one texture. The packer builds both the strip",
        "and the descriptor from this file, so the pixel rectangles cannot drift",
        "out of step with the image.",
        "",
        "'stills' are single frames: the descriptor names the original file and",
        "declares one frame covering it. Nothing is copied.",
        "",
        "Assets that need no processing at all - tiles, power-up icons, sounds -",
        "are not here. Their descriptors are committed under assets/descriptors/",
        "and point straight into the vendored packs.",
        "",
        "The build runs this automatically; by hand it is:",
        "    sif_sprite_packer assets/ assets/sprites.pack.json",
        "    Asset_GUID_Assignment assets/ assets/bin/registry.rgst.json"
    ],

    "output_dir": "graphics/sprites",
    "guid_base": 3000000,

    "animations": [
